# Neon Pairs

Neon Pairs is a memory game that runs offline from one HTML file and keeps local best moves for each board size.

You can repeat a deal with its board code, save progress as a snapshot or run timed actions through the replay command.

Status: implements product spec version 2.2.

## Install

Use the named test combination, Node 26.12.1, npm 11.20.0 and Playwright 1.64.1 with Chromium 156.0.8078.4. From this folder, install the locked tools:

```powershell
npm ci --cache .npm-cache
$env:PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH = Join-Path $PWD '.playwright-browsers'
$env:TEMP = Join-Path $PWD '.browser-work'
$env:TMP = $env:TEMP
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $env:TEMP | Out-Null
npm exec --cache .npm-cache -- playwright install chromium
```

These settings keep the browser download and temporary files inside the project. Browser tests use fresh contexts. They stop their browser and local HTTP server when they finish.

## Play

Run `npm run build`, then open `dist/index.html` from disk. The game makes no network requests. To keep saved sizes and scores on a stable HTTP origin, run `npm run dev`. Stop it when you finish.

Use Grid size to choose a board. Reveal two cards with a click, tap, Enter or Space. Arrow keys move board focus. Other keys stay with the browser. Tab leaves the board. New Game gives another deal. Restart repeats the current deal.

Open Reproduce a game to load a board code or export progress. Loading an unfinished snapshot pauses it. Resume returns focus to the remembered card and continues the remaining mismatch interval. A completed snapshot loads as completed without Resume. Elapsed time stops at 359999999ms while play continues. The minutes and seconds display reaches 5999:59. Moves stop at 999999. Matching and victory continue at that count. Saved bests use the same move limit.

## Replay

Run `npm run --silent replay -- PATH` with a version 1 replay JSON file. Valid input prints only its final version 1 snapshot JSON to stdout and exits 0. Invalid input prints nothing to stdout, writes a message to stderr and exits nonzero. The command's silent flag suppresses its npm banner so stdout stays JSON. Other npm commands keep their errors and warnings. Replay timestamps can reach the safe integer limit. Elapsed time uses the same cap as browser play.

## Check

Run the checks from this folder:

```powershell
npm run typecheck
npm test
$env:NEON_PAIRS_NAMED_COMBINATION = '1'
npm run test:e2e
npm run format:check
```

`npm test` runs the unit and static checks with Vitest 5.0.5. `test:e2e` type checks and builds current source before opening the new HTML. It also builds the face sheet and session harness as separate diagnostic entries. The game distribution contains no diagnostic entry.

The browser command writes the Node, npm, Playwright and Chromium versions it ran on to `test-results/browser-runtime.json`. With `NEON_PAIRS_NAMED_COMBINATION` set to `1`, it also fails unless they match the named combination. Use the flag for named-combination evidence. Other supported runtimes, such as Node 24.19, run without it.

The locked install, type check, Vitest unit tests, build from current source and Chromium journeys have passed on the named combination with the flag set. Other versions have no test record here.

## Accessibility

Keyboard, card names, atomic turn feedback, reduced motion, touch scrolling and the equivalent zoom layout at 640x400 CSS pixels with device scale 2 have browser checks. The diagnostic face sheet draws all 128 faces at 44px.

Playwright checks Chromium's accessibility tree through a complete keyboard journey. It checks controls, card names, states, turn results, the final summary, Tab exit and New Game. The developer provides this tree evidence and the tool record. You confirm spoken output during acceptance with your screen reader.

Tree record: Chromium 156.0.8078.4 and Playwright 1.64.1. Screen reader: not run. Spoken journey: user acceptance.

Delivered projects from document setups keep the product specification in `docs/`.

Follow the requirements in docs/ for this project.
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { test } from 'vitest';
import { activateCard, advanceGame, createGame, MISMATCH_MS, MOVES_MAX } from './game.ts';
import {
  decodeSnapshot,
  encodeSnapshot,
  SNAPSHOT_KEYS,
  SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES,
  SNAPSHOT_VERSION,
} from './snapshot.ts';
import { SelectionKind } from './selection.ts';
import { EXAMPLE_CODE, EXAMPLE_PAIRS, SPEC_VECTOR } from './game.fixture.ts';

function snapshot(overrides: Record<string, unknown> = {}): string {
  return JSON.stringify({
    version: SNAPSHOT_VERSION,
    boardCode: EXAMPLE_CODE,
    matched: [],
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.closed },
    moves: 0,
    elapsedMs: 0,
    started: false,
    ...overrides,
  });
}

test('snapshot round trips preserve pending time and serialize only the declared fields', () => {
  const state = advanceGame(activateCard(activateCard(createGame(EXAMPLE_CODE), 0), 1), 175);
  assert.deepEqual(decodeSnapshot(encodeSnapshot(state)), state);
  assert.deepEqual(state.selection, {
    kind: SelectionKind.mismatch,
    first: 0,
    second: 1,
    remainingMs: MISMATCH_MS - 175,
  });
  assert.equal(SNAPSHOT_VERSION, SPEC_VECTOR.snapshotVersion);
  assert.equal(SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES, SPEC_VECTOR.snapshotBytes);
  const exported: unknown = JSON.parse(encodeSnapshot(state));
  assert.ok(exported && typeof exported === 'object');
  assert.deepEqual(Object.keys(exported).sort(), [...SNAPSHOT_KEYS].sort());
});

test('snapshots accept whole pairs and completed states without changing the source order', () => {
  const state = activateCard(activateCard(createGame(EXAMPLE_CODE), 6), 2);
  assert.deepEqual(decodeSnapshot(encodeSnapshot(state))?.matched, [2, 6]);
  assert.deepEqual(state.matched, [6, 2]);
  assert.equal(
    decodeSnapshot(
      snapshot({ matched: EXAMPLE_PAIRS.flat(), moves: EXAMPLE_PAIRS.length, started: true }),
    )?.matched.length,
    16,
  );
  assert.ok(decodeSnapshot(snapshot({ moves: 17, started: true })));
});

const INVALID_SNAPSHOTS: readonly Record<string, unknown>[] = [
  { extra: true },
  { version: 2 },
  { boardCode: 'np1-4-0' },
  { elapsedMs: -1 },
  { elapsedMs: 0.5 },
  { moves: Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER + 1 },
  { moves: -1 },
  { started: 'true' },
  { matched: [0] },
  { matched: [0, 1] },
  { matched: [2, 6, 2, 6] },
  { matched: [2, 16] },
  { matched: [2, 6], started: true, moves: 0 },
  { selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: 16 }, started: true },
  { selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: 2, extra: true }, started: true },
  { selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: 2 }, started: false },
  { started: true },
  { moves: 1 },
  { elapsedMs: 1 },
  { selection: { kind: 'unknown' } },
  {
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.mismatch, first: 2, second: 6, remainingMs: 1 },
    started: true,
    moves: 1,
  },
  {
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.mismatch, first: 0, second: 0, remainingMs: 1 },
    started: true,
    moves: 1,
  },
  {
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.mismatch, first: 0, second: 1, remainingMs: 0 },
    started: true,
    moves: 1,
  },
  {
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.mismatch, first: 0, second: 1, remainingMs: MISMATCH_MS + 1 },
    started: true,
    moves: 1,
  },
  { matched: [2, 6], selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: 2 }, started: true, moves: 1 },
  { moves: MOVES_MAX + 1, started: true },
];
for (const [index, overrides] of INVALID_SNAPSHOTS.entries()) {
  test(`snapshot validation rejects inconsistent state ${index + 1}`, () => {
    assert.equal(
      decodeSnapshot(snapshot(overrides)),
      null,
      `snapshot rejects isolated field case ${index + 1}`,
    );
  });
}

// Started play with one revealed card is valid at zero moves, so each variant breaks one rule.
const ONE_REVEALED = { started: true, selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: 0 } };
const PENDING = {
  started: true,
  moves: 1,
  selection: { kind: SelectionKind.mismatch, first: 0, second: 1, remainingMs: MISMATCH_MS },
};

test('started progress rejects a nonboolean flag and negative or fractional counters', () => {
  assert.ok(decodeSnapshot(snapshot(ONE_REVEALED)), 'valid started baseline');
  const nonboolean = snapshot({ ...ONE_REVEALED, started: 'true' });
  assert.equal(decodeSnapshot(nonboolean), null, 'nonboolean started');
  for (const field of ['moves', 'elapsedMs'])
    for (const value of [-1, 0.5])
      assert.equal(
        decodeSnapshot(snapshot({ ...ONE_REVEALED, [field]: value })),
        null,
        `${field} must be a nonnegative integer`,
      );
});

test('progress needs one move per matched pair and one for a pending mismatch', () => {
  assert.ok(decodeSnapshot(snapshot(PENDING)), 'valid mismatch baseline');
  const unpaid = snapshot({ ...PENDING, moves: 0 });
  assert.equal(decodeSnapshot(unpaid), null, 'pending mismatch needs one move');
  const twoPairs = {
    ...ONE_REVEALED,
    matched: [2, 6, 0, 11],
    moves: 2,
    selection: { kind: SelectionKind.one, index: 3 },
  };
  assert.ok(decodeSnapshot(snapshot(twoPairs)), 'valid two-pair baseline');
  const short = snapshot({ ...twoPairs, moves: 1 });
  assert.equal(decodeSnapshot(short), null, 'matched pairs need two moves');
});

// Quarter milliseconds are exact in binary.
const BEFORE_MISMATCH_MS = 11;
const INTO_MISMATCH_MS = 0.75;
const NEAR_CLOSE_MS = MISMATCH_MS - 0.25;

test('export writes whole milliseconds and keeps a pending mismatch at 1ms or more', () => {
  const first = activateCard(createGame(EXAMPLE_CODE), 0);
  const mismatch = activateCard(advanceGame(first, BEFORE_MISMATCH_MS), 1);
  for (const milliseconds of [INTO_MISMATCH_MS, NEAR_CLOSE_MS]) {
    const state = advanceGame(mismatch, milliseconds);
    // Import accepts only whole elapsed time and a pending mismatch from 1ms through 800ms.
    const exported = decodeSnapshot(encodeSnapshot(state));
    assert.ok(exported, 'C08 export has whole milliseconds and pending time of at least 1ms');
    assert.ok(Math.abs(exported.elapsedMs - state.elapsedMs) < 1, 'C08 elapsed time is within 1ms');
    assert.ok(
      exported.selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch &&
        state.selection.kind === SelectionKind.mismatch &&
        Math.abs(exported.selection.remainingMs - state.selection.remainingMs) < 1,
      'C08 pending time is within 1ms',
    );
  }
  assert.equal(advanceGame(mismatch, NEAR_CLOSE_MS).selection.kind, SelectionKind.mismatch);
  assert.equal(advanceGame(mismatch, MISMATCH_MS).selection.kind, SelectionKind.closed);
});

test('snapshot parsing enforces malformed, missing and exact byte limits', () => {
  for (const text of ['null', '[]', '{}', '{']) assert.equal(decodeSnapshot(text), null);
  const text = snapshot();
  const padded = text + ' '.repeat(SNAPSHOT_MAX_BYTES - Buffer.byteLength(text));
  assert.ok(decodeSnapshot(padded));
  assert.equal(decodeSnapshot(padded + ' '), null);
});
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { test } from 'vitest';
import { DEAL_NAME_MAX_LENGTH, isValidDealName } from './deal-name.ts';
import { createGame } from './game.ts';
import { decodeSnapshot, encodeSnapshot, SNAPSHOT_KEYS } from './snapshot.ts';
import { EXAMPLE_CODE } from './game.fixture.ts';

test('deal names preserve allowed text and enforce the UTF-16 line rules', () => {
  assert.ok(isValidDealName(''), 'empty name clears the name');
  assert.ok(isValidDealName('  Café ☕  '), 'spaces and Unicode are preserved');
  assert.ok(isValidDealName('Friday run \\ notes'), 'ordinary letters and backslashes remain valid');
  assert.ok(isValidDealName('😀'.repeat(DEAL_NAME_MAX_LENGTH / 2)), 'surrogate pairs count twice');
  assert.equal(isValidDealName('x'.repeat(DEAL_NAME_MAX_LENGTH + 1)), false);
  assert.equal(isValidDealName('line\nbreak'), false);
  assert.equal(isValidDealName('line\rbreak'), false);
});

test('named exports use version 2 and restore their exact names', () => {
  const state = { ...createGame(EXAMPLE_CODE), name: '  Café ☕  ' };
  const value: unknown = JSON.parse(encodeSnapshot(state));
  assert.ok(value && typeof value === 'object');
  assert.equal(Reflect.get(value, 'version'), 2);
  assert.equal(Reflect.get(value, 'name'), state.name);
  assert.deepEqual(decodeSnapshot(encodeSnapshot(state)), state);
});

test('unnamed exports retain the exact version 1 shape and imports clear names', () => {
  const exported: unknown = JSON.parse(encodeSnapshot(createGame(EXAMPLE_CODE)));
  assert.ok(exported && typeof exported === 'object');
  assert.equal(Reflect.get(exported, 'version'), 1);
